Z||000000||Fiero_24||07-20-2001||08:46 AM||||I have a code 35, and I have replaced the EGR, the EGR tube, plugs, wires, coil, module, but I still have the rough idle.  If While the car is idling it starts to stall and then kicks back up.  If I start driving it seems like it wants to stall when I stop for the first minute or two.  I still get the code 35.  I did take the Idle Air Control out and I cleaned it and the throttle body, still nothing.  I was told by a local autopart store that it could be the IAC, or the Map sensor.  I would think more the IAC, but if anything I though this would have beeen fixed.  After driving for a while the RPM gauge starts to jump from 800 to 1500 really fast back and forth at stop lights.  I do not notice anything during driving at all.  Before I changed the ignition module it missed all through driving speeds.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||8
Z||000001||Voytek||07-20-2001||02:10 PM||||I've had a somewhat similar problem recently.  The idle would start dropping and rising, but each time it dropped it went lower until the car would almost stall.  Then it would jump back up fairly high, stay there for a second and equalize again.  It would go through this cycle all the time.  I took it to a shop and it turned out that the timing was misadjusted by 5 degrees.  They also hooked up a computer and programmed the correct idle speed into the ECM.<BR>Sometimes this can be caused by worn timing / distributor components.  I'd try the diagnostic first.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
